'''Pelliaceae''' is a [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] of [[Marchantiophyta|liverworts]] which has included three genera: ''[[Pellia]]'' (in the temperate Northern Hemisphere) and ''[[Noteroclada]]'' (in the Southern Hemisphere), and ''[[Androcryphia]]''.  The three genera are easily distinguished, not only because they occur in completely separate regions of the world, but because ''Noteroclada'' has a leafy appearance, while ''Pellia'' is more clearly [[thallus (tissue)|thallose]]. ''Androcryphia'' is much less common, and bears similarities to the [[folio]]se members of [[Jungermanniales]]. ''Noteroclada'' is now placed in the family [[Noterocladaceae]].

